            classified by the cocycle.
          %p
            It is now evident that our discussion of ordinary smooth principal bundles
            %a{:href => "#PrincipalBundles"} above
            is the special case of this for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of the one-object groupoid associated with the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
